## Architecture

Hunter consumes market data and exchange services through the shared `classified` package.

```text
Hunter
   |
   v
ClassifiedMarketDataGateway
   |
   v
Classified MarketDataManager
   |
   v
ExchangeAdapter / CCXT
   |
   v
BingX
```

Hunter does not import CCXT or communicate directly with BingX. Exchange connectivity, market-data retrieval, and standardized candle delivery remain behind the Classified integration boundary.

Hunter owns its analytical requirements and liquidity-processing logic. This separation prevents Hunter from duplicating the shared market-data infrastructure.

### Market-data requirements

Hunter's default candle requirements are:

| Timeframe | Candle count | Purpose |
|---|---:|---|
| 4H | 200 | Macro context |
| 1H | 300 | Intermediate context |
| 15M | 400 | Setup development |
| 5M | 500 | Execution context |

These are Hunter-specific defaults, not hard limits imposed by Classified. They can be adjusted as the strategy and analytical requirements evolve.

The gateway supports both single-timeframe and multi-timeframe requests while preserving the standardized candle model.

