## Backtesting

Hunter includes a deterministic backtesting engine that is separate from the paper/live runtime. Liquidity events are not automatically treated as trading signals.

The engine supports:

- Risk-based position sizing.
- Structural stop-loss and target levels supplied by a setup policy.
- Trading fees and slippage.
- Daily loss limits.
- Consecutive-loss limits.
- Missed and unfinished entry handling.
- Explicit OHLCV ambiguity policies.
- Trade-level R-multiples and PnL.
- Fee and slippage accounting.
- Drawdown and losing-streak metrics.

Backtests should be validated out of sample. Finer-grained execution data is necessary when intrabar sequencing materially affects the outcome.

The engine does not invent a closing trade at the end of a dataset simply to force completion.

Backtesting results do not guarantee live trading performance.

